<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">Tyranny of Pherae</h1><p class="st-meta">406 BCE – 352 BCE (approx.) · capital Pherae</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Line of ambitious tyrants in the Thessalian city of Pherae who briefly made Thessaly a great power under Jason before falling to Philip II.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Pherae, in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thessaly">Thessaly</a> near the port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pagasae">Pagasae</a>, rose against the old aristocratic families of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/larissa">Larissa</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/pharsalus">Pharsalus</a>. Around 406 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lycophron-of-pherae">Lycophron of Pherae</a> seized power and tried to dominate all of Thessaly, defeating his rivals in 404 BCE. His successor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jason-of-pherae">Jason</a> built a large <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenary</a> army and was elected tagos, leader of the Thessalian federation, around 374 BCE.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The tyrants depended on paid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a>, the port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pagasae">Pagasae</a> and alliances with outside powers. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jason-of-pherae">Jason</a> planned a fleet and even, according to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xenophon">Xenophon</a>, a campaign against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a>, but was assassinated in 370 BCE. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-of-pherae">Alexander of Pherae</a> (369-358 BCE) was notorious for cruelty and fought <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/thebes">Thebes</a>, killing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pelopidas">Pelopidas</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-cynoscephalae-364-bce">Cynoscephalae</a> in 364 BCE though losing the battle.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Alexander was murdered by his wife <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thebe-of-pherae">Thebe</a> and her brothers, who ruled in turn. Their struggle with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/thessalian-league">Thessalian League</a> brought in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-macedon">Philip II of Macedon</a>, who defeated the Phocian allies of Pherae at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-crocus-field">Crocus Field</a> in 352 BCE and expelled the tyrants. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thessaly">Thessaly</a> then came under Macedonian control.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 406 BCE – 352 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">city state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Greece and the Aegean</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:51.62%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>406 BCE – 352 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Pherae</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Lycophron, Jason of Pherae, Alexander of Pherae</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Ancient Greek religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Ancient Greek (Thessalian)</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/greece">Greece</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Pherae</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-379&amp;focus=tyranny-of-pherae" aria-label="Tyranny of Pherae on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5242 767 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Tyranny of Pherae lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5562 1023L5553 1014M5562 1023L5548 987"/><path cla